DadaSafe Dashboard

A web-based administration and support management dashboard for the DadaSafe platform.

DadaSafe is a digital safety platform designed to educate young women in Kenya about digital safety, online risks, and responsible digital practices. The platform also provides a support pathway for users who have experienced cyberbullying or other technology-related challenges by connecting them with mental health and support providers.

The DadaSafe Dashboard provides the management and support infrastructure required to operate these services. It consists of two main dashboard environments: the Admin Dashboard and the Support Provider Dashboard.

The Admin Dashboard is designed for administrators responsible for managing the platform, monitoring user activity, generating educational games, managing game content, and overseeing support-related information.

The Support Provider Dashboard is designed for authorized support providers who manage incoming support requests. Support providers can view submitted cases, access the user's available contact information, review problem descriptions, track when requests were submitted, and update the status of support requests as they are handled.

Both dashboards are implemented within the same frontend application and are separated through Next.js routing, allowing each type of authorized user to access the appropriate dashboard area while maintaining a shared application structure and codebase.


DadaSafe Dashboard is the web-based management interface for the DadaSafe platform.

The dashboard functions as the frontend management layer of the system. It provides authorized administrators and support providers with interfaces for interacting with information stored and managed by the DadaSafe backend.

The frontend communicates with the backend through RESTful API endpoints. Backend services are responsible for database operations, authentication, authorization, business logic, support requests, user records, and game information, while the dashboard is responsible for presenting this information and allowing authorized users to perform supported actions.

The application is divided into two main areas:

DadaSafe Dashboard
│
├── Admin Dashboard
│   ├── Dashboard
│   ├── Settings
│   ├── User Management
│   ├── Game Management
│   ├── AI Game Generation
│   └── Game Preview
│
└── Support Dashboard
    ├── Dashboard
    ├── Support Requests
    ├── Case Statistics
    ├── Case Status Management
    ├── Profile
    └── Settings

The two areas are combined within the same Next.js project and separated through application routing.

# Key Features
## Administration

The Admin Dashboard provides administrators with tools for managing the educational and operational aspects of the DadaSafe platform.

Administrative functionality includes:

Administrator dashboard
Platform activity monitoring
User registration information
User management
User suspension
User banning
Administrative settings
Support case statistics
Game generation
Game management
Game payload management
Game preview
JSON payload editing
JSON validation
JSON formatting
Theme selection
Topic selection
AI-assisted game generation
Administrator profile functionality
Administrator logout

## Support Management

The Support Provider Dashboard provides authorized support providers with tools for managing support requests submitted by users.

Support functionality includes:

Support dashboard
Total support request count
Pending request count
In-progress request count
Attended request count
Support request table
User email display
Optional phone number display
Problem description display
Request submission date
Request status updates
Request priority management
Search functionality
Support profile
Support settings
Theme support
Support-provider logout

The terminology presented in the frontend uses:

pending
in_progress
attended


# Technology Stack
## Frontend Technologies
Technology	Purpose
Next.js	Frontend framework, routing, application structure, and production builds
React	Component-based user interface development
JavaScript	Application logic
JSX	React component markup
Tailwind CSS	Utility-based styling and responsive layouts
CSS	Custom dashboard styling
Lucide React	Interface icons
TanStack Form	Form state and form submission management
Fetch API	Communication with REST APIs
Next.js

The dashboard is built using Next.js, which provides the main application framework and routing structure.

The project uses the Next.js App Router approach to organize pages and dashboard sections.

Examples of application routes include:

/admin/dashboard
/admin/settings
/admin/control

/support/dashboard
/support/profile

Routing allows both dashboards to exist inside the same project while maintaining separate navigation structures and functionality.
Application Architecture

The DadaSafe Dashboard follows a component-based frontend architecture using Next.js and React.

The application is divided into pages, reusable components, API utility modules, hooks, and dashboard-specific layouts.

The main application areas are separated using Next.js routing:

Admin
/admin/dashboard
/admin/settings
/admin/control

Support
/support/dashboard
/support/profile
/support/settings

Each dashboard has its own navigation and interface while sharing the same frontend project.

The application communicates with the FastAPI backend through REST API requests. Components retrieve backend data, display it to users, and send updates back to the backend when an authorized action is performed.

Dashboard Layout

The dashboard interface uses a consistent sidebar-based layout.

The sidebar provides navigation between the available sections of each dashboard. The current route is detected using Next.js routing so that the active navigation item can be visually highlighted.

The main content area contains the functionality associated with the selected page.

Common interface elements include:

Sidebar navigation
Dashboard cards
Statistics
Tables
Forms
Dropdown menus
Search fields
Status controls
Loading states
Error states
Profile sections
Action buttons

The dashboard uses reusable React components to avoid duplicating interface logic across different pages.

Admin Dashboard

The Admin Dashboard provides administrators with centralized control over the DadaSafe platform.

The dashboard allows administrators to monitor platform information and manage users and educational game content.

The main administrative sections include:

Dashboard

Provides an overview of important platform statistics and activity.

Settings

Provides administrative controls for managing registered users.

Administrators can:

View registered users
Select users from the database
Ban users
Suspend users
Provide reasons for administrative actions

These actions are submitted to the backend through API requests.

Control

The control area provides functionality related to managing and generating educational game content.

Navigation

Administrators can move between dashboard sections using the sidebar.

A logout option is also provided to allow administrators to end their authenticated session.

Support Provider Dashboard

The Support Provider Dashboard is designed for authorized support providers who handle support requests submitted through DadaSafe.

The dashboard provides an overview of support activity and allows providers to manage individual requests.

The support dashboard displays:

Total support requests
Pending requests
In-progress requests
Attended requests

Support requests are displayed in a structured table.

Each request can contain:

User email
Optional phone number
Problem description
Submission date
Current status
Priority

Support providers can update the status of a request as they handle it.

The frontend uses the terminology:

pending
in_progress
attended

The backend represents attended using the resolved status value. The frontend therefore presents the status as attended while maintaining compatibility with the backend status representation.

Support Request Management

Support requests are retrieved from the backend and displayed dynamically on the Support Dashboard.

The support request table provides search functionality, allowing support providers to search for cases based on their problem descriptions.

Each request has a status selector that allows authorized support providers to update the request status.

The frontend sends the selected status to the backend through the support request API.

Support providers can also manage the priority associated with a case through the priority selector.

The support request interface is designed to provide the information required for a provider to identify and follow up on a support case.

Game Management

The Admin Dashboard includes functionality for managing educational games used by the DadaSafe platform.

Game information is retrieved from the backend and displayed through administrative interfaces.

Administrators can work with:

Game titles
Game topics
Game themes
Game payloads
Quiz content
Scenario content
Generated game content

The dashboard also provides a preview interface for viewing game content before it is used by the platform.

Topic Selection

The game-generation interface allows administrators to select an educational theme and a related topic.

Themes are mapped to predefined topics within the frontend.

For example, themes can include:

Location Tracking & Surveillance Countermeasures
Image-Based Abuse & Media Violations
Device Security & Spyware Mitigation
Social Media & Online Platform Safety
Legal Protections, Evidence, & Policy
Account Security & Digital Hygiene

After selecting a theme, the topic selector displays topics associated with that theme.

This prevents unrelated topics from being selected for a particular educational theme.

AI Game Generation

The dashboard provides an interface for generating educational game content using an AI-assisted workflow.

The administrator selects a theme and topic and then provides instructions through the prompt interface.

The prompt component validates the input before submitting it to the game-generation process.

The generated game data can then be displayed and reviewed through the dashboard.

The generation workflow is designed to allow administrators to create educational content while maintaining control over the selected subject area.

Game Preview

The Game Preview component provides an interface for viewing generated game content in a simulated mobile-style environment.

Game data is retrieved from the backend using the game identifier.

The preview can display information such as:

Game title
Game topic
Quiz content
Scenario content
Game session information

The preview allows administrators to inspect generated content before making further changes or updates.

JSON Editor

The dashboard includes a JSON editor for viewing and editing game payloads.

The editor converts JavaScript objects into formatted JSON for display.

When editing is enabled, administrators can modify the JSON directly.

The editor validates the JSON whenever the content changes.

If invalid JSON is entered, an error message is displayed and the invalid payload is prevented from being treated as valid data.

The editor also provides a formatting function that converts valid JSON into a readable, properly indented structure.

Authentication and Authorization

Authentication is handled through the DadaSafe backend.

Users authenticate through the login system and receive an authentication token.

The frontend stores and retrieves the token when making authenticated requests to protected backend endpoints.

Administrative and support functionality is separated according to the user's authorized role.

Protected backend endpoints are responsible for verifying whether the authenticated user has permission to perform a requested action.

The frontend also provides logout functionality that removes the relevant authentication information and redirects the user to the login page.

Backend Integration

The DadaSafe Dashboard communicates with a FastAPI backend.

The backend is responsible for:

User authentication
User registration
Authorization
Database operations
Support requests
User management
Game data
Game updates
Administrative operations

The dashboard acts as the client application that consumes these backend services.

For example, the Support Dashboard retrieves support requests from the backend and displays them in the case table.

When a support provider changes a case status, the frontend sends the update to the backend, where the request is validated and stored.

